# Copy to .env.document-pipeline next to the compose file (mode 600). Names and placeholders only: this example holds no key, no secret and no usable token (SERVICE_AUTH_HEADER is empty here).
# The copy holds two keys, the supplier key (the runtime's) and the buyer key (the service's), and the token between the two containers, and it never enters git: the repository's .gitignore covers .env.* except *.example.
# Status: DEPLOYED since 2026-10-16. The status word the manifest carries is AGENT_STATUS_CHIP below.
# The external network of the host's reverse proxy is not named here: compose reads PROXY_NETWORK from .env next to the compose file (RUNBOOK-document-pipeline.md step 1).
# Identity of the supplier (from the first gen-keypair on the box, RUNBOOK-document-pipeline.md step 4). The runtime signs the receipt over the bundle with this key.
SUPPLIER_PRIV_KEY_HEX=
SUPPLIER_PUB_KEY_HEX=
SUPPLIER_PKH=
SUPPLIER_ADDRESS=
# The buyer (from the second gen-keypair, same step). The service posts the escrows of the sub-jobs it hires with this key. It is a separate key, so that the service's Posts and the supplier key's Claims never contend for the same outputs.
# The runtime does not get it: the compose file blanks it there. The service derives the key hash and the address from the key and stops at start when PIPELINE_BUYER_PKH or PIPELINE_BUYER_ADDRESS says something else.
PIPELINE_BUYER_PRIV_KEY_HEX=
PIPELINE_BUYER_PUB_KEY_HEX=
PIPELINE_BUYER_PKH=
PIPELINE_BUYER_ADDRESS=
# The token between the two containers (ruling R50). The runtime sends this value, as it stands, as the authorization header of every call to the service, and the service answers POST / only to a call that carries it.
# Both containers read it from this file and neither blanks it. Step 4 makes it with openssl rand -hex 32, in the form SERVICE_AUTH_HEADER="Bearer <64 hex>" (71 characters).
# The quotes are needed: the ops scripts read this file with the shell's ".", and an unquoted value with a space in it would run the hex as a command and stop with exit 127. Docker Compose takes the quotes off.
# Empty here on purpose: the service stops at start without it (environment variable SERVICE_AUTH_HEADER is required), so a step that was forgotten cannot leave a service that answers anyone.
SERVICE_AUTH_HEADER=""
# Chain
NETWORK_ID=1
OGMIOS_URL=https://ogmios.vector.mainnet.apexfusion.org
VECTOR_ZERO_TIME_MS=1756485600000
LIVE_CHAIN=1
ESCROW_REF_UTXO=c8d84c6d67ec67a1efe5e9c6c06d53020e05d1bb96d1c55ecb1eb7d5010c4d54#0
ADVERT_REF_UTXO=c8d84c6d67ec67a1efe5e9c6c06d53020e05d1bb96d1c55ecb1eb7d5010c4d54#1
# The escrow and the advert that carry an agent_id (the runtime): the reference scripts that the identity registry deployment on Vector mainnet published
# on 2026-11-03. Keep ESCROW_REF_UTXO and ADVERT_REF_UTXO above while legacy escrows exist. The runtime works an escrow that names the agent only with
# IDENTITY_POLICY_ID (below) and AGENT_ID, the identifier of the agent's record (64 hex): the step that makes the record writes AGENT_ID into this file.
IDENTITY_ESCROW_REF_UTXO=4c2d09858dab0cc22cc77dcb99efed570d909a66e0beb512041dea91005b5e82#0
IDENTITY_ADVERT_REF_UTXO=5efd18a1d90a6b87f1fd4b6fe93acfbe5be082260fd52be194b1088ade7c2758#0
# The identity registry deployment, for the escrows the service posts: packages/buyer-core reads these three lines. They hold the values that the deployment
# on Vector mainnet published on 2026-11-03; empty lines mean legacy adverts and escrows only. VECTOR_IDENTITY_LEGACY_ROOT (the Merkle root of the adoption allowlist, 64 hex characters) and
# VECTOR_IDENTITY_CONFIG_SEED (the seed output of the configuration seal, <txid>#<index>) are its two deployment values, under the names the MCP server reads: set both or neither.
# With them the service can hire through the adverts of the identity marketplace and settle their escrows, and IDENTITY_POLICY_ID below must be the identity policy they give,
# or the service stops at start and names the variables. A value that breaks a rule stops the start, and the error names the variable.
VECTOR_IDENTITY_LEGACY_ROOT=e4b6b17ce4a8f83aa17d3181ea140d2bd76c0cfa8a7c44ad69543800b4a0df01
VECTOR_IDENTITY_CONFIG_SEED=6c9856c70b1101f1a4e9ceb373188608013416eff48c51f5bb62706a65d41a2a#0
# VECTOR_IDENTITY_ESCROW_REF_UTXO: the reference-script UTxO of the escrow of the identity marketplace, <64 hex>#<index>. The Accept and the Reclaim of such an escrow need it, so it is required with the two values above.
VECTOR_IDENTITY_ESCROW_REF_UTXO=4c2d09858dab0cc22cc77dcb99efed570d909a66e0beb512041dea91005b5e82#0
# Advert (filled by post-advert)
ADVERT_REF=
ADVERT_CAPABILITY_ID=document.pipeline.ocr-summary.v1
ADVERT_MODEL=document-pipeline-v1
ADVERT_PRICE_LOVELACE=5000000
ADVERT_SUPPLIER_BOND_LOVELACE=1000000
ADVERT_BUYER_BOND_LOVELACE=1000000
ADVERT_MAX_PROCESSING_MS=1800000
ADVERT_ENDPOINT_URL=https://mp-suppliers-pipeline.hal8.ai
ADVERT_DETAIL_URI=https://mp-suppliers-pipeline.hal8.ai/agent.json
ADVERT_DETAIL_HASH=
# Manifest (service). What the service serves at /agent.json is hashed into the advert, so every line in this block, ADVERT_PRICE_LOVELACE and ADVERT_MAX_PROCESSING_MS above (the manifest publishes both as its terms),
# and the identity lines above (the supplier key hash and public key, the buyer key hash), must be final before the hash is taken. A change afterwards means a retired advert and a new one.
# Left unset on purpose: AGENT_VERSION (the service has its own default), and VECTOR_MARKETPLACE_INDEXER_URL, VECTOR_OGMIOS_URL, VECTOR_KOIOS_URL and VECTOR_SUBMIT_URL (the defaults of the code are Vector mainnet's).
# OPERATOR_CONTACT is required: the service stops at start without it, and the value is published in the manifest. There is no default. Replace the
# placeholder with the role address the Foundation confirms, never a person's address (RUNBOOK-document-pipeline.md step 4, "Make the env file and generate the two keys").
OPERATOR_CONTACT=<role address, e.g. ecosystem@<foundation domain>; the Foundation confirms which>
# AGENT_DID is written by the register step (RUNBOOK-document-pipeline.md step 7, "Register the identity"), which refuses to run while this empty line is here. Remove the line first.
AGENT_DID=
# IDENTITY_POLICY_ID: the policy ID of the identity registry, 56 lowercase hex characters, as its deployment publishes it: here the policy that the deployment on
# Vector mainnet published on 2026-11-03. The runtime reads it too. Empty: the identity registry is not configured.
# The manifest publishes the address of this policy as identity.registry_address, empty while this line is empty. With the two deployment values above, it must be the policy they give.
IDENTITY_POLICY_ID=d958b823faaa76977d0a07bd9622e87d8e2c85f6692f7f8e8db77762
# IDENTITY_ADDRESS: the address of the identity registry. Empty means the address of IDENTITY_POLICY_ID. A value needs IDENTITY_POLICY_ID and must be the address of that policy.
IDENTITY_ADDRESS=
# The status word the manifest carries, and since when: deployed since 2026-10-16, after the advert was Active and a first-party job had settled (RUNBOOK-document-pipeline.md step 17, "Flip the status"). A first-party run is not demand, so the word is not live.
# On a first run, before any job has settled, set proposed and today's date here; step 17 changes them.
AGENT_STATUS_CHIP=deployed
AGENT_STATUS_SINCE=2026-10-16
# Stays empty: the advert's own transaction id cannot be inside the manifest the advert hashes.
ADVERT_EXPLORER_URL=
# What the Pipeline hires (service). Both lines are the defaults of the code, written here so that a change is visible and reviewed.
# The OCR supplier is one first-party key hash, which is public and not ours. The Pipeline posts to the one Active OCR advert of that key, and to no other.
# The chat models are the ones it may hire for the summary or the extraction, comma separated, in order of preference.
OCR_ALLOWLIST_SUPPLIER_PKH=401af418a7e6fb106277292881fcdeaa1cc15b5b112e9c8bdb2d46c9
LLM_MODEL_ALLOWLIST=deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash,deepseek-v4-pro,moonshotai/kimi-k2.6,Qwen/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-FP8
# The most an OCR page and the chat job may each be priced at, in lovelace. An advert priced above its ceiling is not hired: the job is refused with
# ocr_supplier_unavailable or llm_supplier_unavailable (503) before it locks anything. Left commented: these are the defaults of the code. A higher
# ceiling takes a larger float, which each job checks again before its first Post.
# OCR_MAX_PRICE_LOVELACE=1000000
# LLM_MAX_PRICE_LOVELACE=1000000
